# slurm-shim @VERSION@

This directory holds the latest slurm-shim release, the same files as on the
[GitHub release page](https://github.com/hpc-gridware/slurm-shim/releases/tag/@VERSION@):

| File | |
|---|---|
| `slurm-shim_linux_amd64.tar.gz` | x86-64 cluster nodes |
| `slurm-shim_linux_arm64.tar.gz` | ARM64 cluster nodes |
| `SHA256SUMS` | checksums of both |

Third-party licenses and the SBOM of this release are in the
`3rdparty-licenses` directory of the repository; the SBOM is also attached to
the release as `sbom.cyclonedx.json`.

## Install

Run as an Open Cluster Scheduler and Gridware Cluster Scheduler manager on a
host that shares `$SGE_ROOT` with the cluster nodes.

```bash
source $SGE_ROOT/default/common/settings.sh
sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing

mkdir -p $SGE_ROOT/slurm-shim
tar -xzf slurm-shim_linux_amd64.tar.gz -C $SGE_ROOT/slurm-shim

$SGE_ROOT/slurm-shim/bin/slurm-shim install                    # prints the plan, changes nothing
$SGE_ROOT/slurm-shim/bin/slurm-shim install --apply --expose=profile.d
$SGE_ROOT/slurm-shim/bin/slurm-shim doctor
```

`install --apply` creates the PE `slurm-shim` and a queue of its own,
`slurm.q`, and changes no existing queue. `--queue all` wires every existing
queue instead. `--expose=module` writes a modulefile instead of
`/etc/profile.d/slurm-shim.sh`.

## Uninstall

```bash
$SGE_ROOT/slurm-shim/bin/slurm-shim uninstall                  # prints the plan, changes nothing
$SGE_ROOT/slurm-shim/bin/slurm-shim uninstall --apply
```

Uninstall undoes what install did and removes the installed files. It keeps the
config; `--purge-config` removes it too. It changes nothing while a job still
uses the shim.

## Config outside `$SGE_ROOT`

`install --apply --config PATH`, or `--config-dir DIR` for a Qontrol config
dir, keeps the config out of `$SGE_ROOT` so a scheduler reinstall does not
delete it. Put it on shared storage: every submit and exec host reads it at
the same path. `slurm-shim config path` shows which file is in use.

More information, including configuration, upgrades and troubleshooting:
https://github.com/hpc-gridware/slurm-shim

